In the-game-that-nethack-is-not (at least the latest version), magic is 
verbal and need gesture, unless you spend some points to cast spells 
without speaking and without moving hands. This is also the case is some 
other magical RPG (typically, Ars Magica) and seems, to me, to be a 
fairly common "folk knowledge".

In nethack (well, slash'em), how is this handled ?
I know that you cannot cast spell while having both of your hands 
wielded to a cursed item, so that suggest that magic needs gestures. 
However, you can cast spell in a non-speaking form (my current crystal 
golem cannot #chat ("having no mouth you cannot speak" or something 
similar) but can cast spells fairly well). So, that would mean that 
magic is non-verbal (and that a spell/item providing some kind of 
"silence sphere" (could be a nice addition to the Heart) will only help 
on the stealth level but not hamper spellcasters).

What I've not tried (yeah, I should have before posting) is to cast 
spells with a handless form (a g-cube, or something else).

So, the questionis to know if NH-magic need gestures/speach/both/none.

The naturally-related YANI(s) is to prevent monsters in 
non-speaking/handless form to cast spells. Maybe to have some classes 
allowed to do speachless/gestureless magic (or this might be a skill to 
buy with skill points). Then, you may have a spell/item causing some 
kind of silence sphere around you, and high-level nasty spellcasters 
would have the skill to cast silent magic. Even worse, you may want to 
allow gestureless spellcasters to cast spells with both hands wielded to 
  an item, or while being grabbed by something, or even at early stage 
of stoning/paralysis (supposing that the process first affect your body 
and then your brain/mind).


